    "Run the health check below and confirm it passes before creating any schema.",
    "Apply the generated schema/config (table + vector index, or collection/index config) exactly as reviewed - do not hand-edit generated identifiers.",
    "Re-run the health check after schema creation to confirm the database is still reachable and responsive.",
    "Record this deployment (version, rules version, timestamp) in the audit trail before marking Phase 4 complete.",
  ],
  "healthCheck": {
    "check": "SELECT 1",
    "description": "Execute a trivial query against the target PostgreSQL instance.",
  },
  "kubernetes": {
    "helmValuesYaml": "# Values for the official \`milvus/milvus\` Helm chart (helm repo add milvus https://zilliztech.github.io/milvus-helm/).
# helm install enterprise_docs_milvus milvus/milvus -n enterprise_docs_milvus -f these-values.yaml
cluster:
  enabled: true
etcd:
  replicaCount: 3
  persistence:
    enabled: true
    size: 10Gi
minio:
  mode: distributed
  persistence:
    enabled: true
    size: 100Gi
  existingSecret: milvus-credentials
pulsar:
  enabled: true
queryNode:
  replicas: 2
dataNode:
  replicas: 2
indexNode:
  replicas: 2
proxy:
  replicas: 2
metrics:
  enabled: true
  serviceMonitor:
    enabled: true # scraped by Prometheus - see the health check / monitoring notes",
    "namespaceYaml": "apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: enterprise_docs_milvus",
    "notes": [
      "Query/data/index node and proxy replica counts are starting points - size per the Phase 3 index choice and expected QPS, then revisit in Phase 7 (Scaling & Sharding).",
      "Persistent volume sizes must exceed the Phase 3 Indexing Strategy Guide’s estimated memory/storage footprint with headroom for growth.",
    ],
    "secretYaml": "apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: milvus-credentials
  namespace: enterprise_docs_milvus
type: Opaque
stringData:
  # Never commit real values - populate via \`kubectl create secret\` or a secrets manager (e.g. External Secrets Operator).
  MINIO_ACCESS_KEY: "REPLACE_ME"
  MINIO_SECRET_KEY: "REPLACE_ME"",
  },
  "rollback": [
    "Never run a destructive rollback step (dropping a table/collection, deleting a cluster) without explicit, out-of-band confirmation - the adapter layer refuses drop operations unless confirm=true is passed deliberately.",
    "Prefer disabling traffic to the new schema/collection (feature flag or app-config rollback) over deleting data, so the failed deployment can be inspected afterward.",
    "Restore the RDS/Cloud SQL instance from its automatic snapshot to the timestamp immediately before this deployment.",
    "If only the vector index is at fault, DROP INDEX (not the table) and re-run Phase 3 tuning before recreating it.",
  ],
  "terraform": "# STARTING POINT - fill in VPC/subnet/sizing for your AWS account before applying.
resource "aws_db_instance" "golden_master_project" {
  identifier              = "golden_master_project"
  engine                  = "postgres"
  engine_version          = var.postgres_engine_version # must be >= 15 for current pgvector
  instance_class          = var.instance_class
  allocated_storage       = var.allocated_storage_gb
  username                = "vector_admin"
  password                = var.db_admin_password # supply via TF_VAR_/secret manager - never commit
  db_subnet_group_name    = var.db_subnet_group_name
  vpc_security_group_ids  = var.vpc_security_group_ids
  skip_final_snapshot     = false
  final_snapshot_identifier = "golden_master_project-final"
}

variable "postgres_engine_version" {
  type    = string
  default = "16.4"
}
variable "instance_class" {
  type    = string
  default = "db.r6g.large"
}
variable "allocated_storage_gb" {
  type    = number
  default = 100
}
variable "db_admin_password" {
  type      = string
  sensitive = true
}
variable "db_subnet_group_name" {
  type = string
}
variable "vpc_security_group_ids" {
  type = list(string)
}

# Run once connected: CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector; (see the generated SQL script).",
}
`;

exports[`Golden master - existing VectorDB workflow (must not change unintentionally) Phase 5 - deployment artefacts for every platform IaC and runbooks: qdrant 1`] = `
{
  "checklist": [
    "Provision the Kubernetes cluster via the generated Terraform (or an existing cluster).",
    "Create the namespace and secrets from the generated Kubernetes YAML.",
    "\`helm install\` (or apply the custom resource, for Elasticsearch/ECK) using the generated values file.",
    "Wait for all pods to reach Ready.",
    "Confirm TARGET_* connection environment variables are set via a secret manager, never committed to source control.",
    "Verify network connectivity (VPC peering / security group / firewall rule, or API reachability for a SaaS platform) from the application to the target database.",
    "Run the health check below and confirm it passes before creating any schema.",
    "Apply the generated schema/config (table + vector index, or collection/index config) exactly as reviewed - do not hand-edit generated identifiers.",
    "Re-run the health check after schema creation to confirm the database is still reachable and responsive.",
    "Record this deployment (version, rules version, timestamp) in the audit trail before marking Phase 4 complete.",
  ],
  "healthCheck": {
    "check": "GET /healthz",
    "description": "Call Qdrant's health endpoint and confirm a 200 response.",
  },
  "kubernetes": {
    "helmValuesYaml": "# Values for the official \`qdrant/qdrant\` Helm chart (helm repo add qdrant https://qdrant.github.io/qdrant-helm).
# helm install enterprise_docs_qdrant qdrant/qdrant -n enterprise_docs_qdrant -f these-values.yaml
replicaCount: 3
persistence:
  size: 50Gi
apiKey:
  existingSecret: qdrant-api-key
  existingSecretKey: QDRANT__SERVICE__API_KEY
service:
  type: ClusterIP",
    "namespaceYaml": "apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: enterprise_docs_qdrant",
    "notes": [
      "replicaCount and persistence size are starting points - size per the Phase 3 index choice and expected vector count/QPS.",
      "Qdrant shards collections automatically across replicas when created with shard_number > 1 - set that at collection-creation time (Phase 2 schema), not here.",
    ],
    "secretYaml": "apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: qdrant-api-key
  namespace: enterprise_docs_qdrant
type: Opaque
stringData:
  # Never commit real values - populate via \`kubectl create secret\` or a secrets manager.
  QDRANT__SERVICE__API_KEY: "REPLACE_ME"",
  },
  "rollback": [
    "Never run a destructive rollback step (dropping a table/collection, deleting a cluster) without explicit, out-of-band confirmation - the adapter layer refuses drop operations unless confirm=true is passed deliberately.",
    "Prefer disabling traffic to the new schema/collection (feature flag or app-config rollback) over deleting data, so the failed deployment can be inspected afterward.",
    "Roll back with \`helm rollback <release> <previous-revision>\` rather than deleting the namespace.",
    "If only the collection’s/index's configuration is at fault, drop and recreate just the index rather than the collection.",
  ],
  "terraform": "# STARTING POINT - provisions the Kubernetes cluster qdrant will run on.
# Fill in node sizing/count and networking for your cloud provider before applying.
resource "google_container_cluster" "golden_master_project" {
  name     = "golden_master_project-qdrant"
  location = var.gcp_region

  node_pool {
    name       = "qdrant-pool"
    node_count = var.node_count
    node_config {
      machine_type = var.machine_type
    }
  }
}

variable "gcp_region" {
  type = string
}
variable "node_count" {
  type    = number
  default = 3
}
variable "machine_type" {
  type    = string
  default = "e2-standard-8"
}

# Deploy qdrant itself onto this cluster with Helm/K8s YAML - see the generated Kubernetes artifacts.",
}
`;

exports[`Golden master - existing VectorDB workflow (must not change unintentionally) Phase 5 - deployment artefacts for every platform IaC and runbooks: redis 1`] = `
{
  "checklist": [
    "Provision the Kubernetes cluster via the generated Terraform (or an existing cluster).",
    "Create the namespace and secrets from the generated Kubernetes YAML.",
    "\`helm install\` (or apply the custom resource, for Elasticsearch/ECK) using the generated values file.",
    "Wait for all pods to reach Ready.",
    "Confirm TARGET_* connection environment variables are set via a secret manager, never committed to source control.",
    "Verify network connectivity (VPC peering / security group / firewall rule, or API reachability for a SaaS platform) from the application to the target database.",
    "Run the health check below and confirm it passes before creating any schema.",
    "Apply the generated schema/config (table + vector index, or collection/index config) exactly as reviewed - do not hand-edit generated identifiers.",
    "Re-run the health check after schema creation to confirm the database is still reachable and responsive.",
    "Record this deployment (version, rules version, timestamp) in the audit trail before marking Phase 4 complete.",
  ],
  "healthCheck": {
    "check": "PING",
    "description": "Send a PING and confirm a PONG response.",
  },
  "kubernetes": {
    "helmValuesYaml": "# Standard managed Redis (e.g. AWS ElastiCache) does NOT support vector search - this uses the Bitnami \`redis\`
# chart with the image overridden to \`redis-stack-server\`, which bundles the RediSearch module.
# helm repo add bitnami https://charts.bitnami.com/bitnami && helm install enterprise_docs_redis bitnami/redis -n enterprise_docs_redis -f these-values.yaml
image:
  repository: redis/redis-stack-server
  tag: latest
auth:
  existingSecret: redis-credentials
  existingSecretPasswordKey: REDIS_PASSWORD
master:
  persistence:
    size: 20Gi
replica:
  replicaCount: 2
  persistence:
    size: 20Gi",
    "namespaceYaml": "apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: enterprise_docs_redis",
    "notes": [
      "Plain open-source Redis and standard managed Redis (AWS ElastiCache, etc.) do not support vector search - only Redis Stack (self-hosted, shown here) or Redis Enterprise Cloud (fully managed) include the RediSearch module.",
      "replica count and persistence size are starting points - size per the Phase 3 index choice and expected vector count/QPS.",
    ],
    "secretYaml": "apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: redis-credentials
  namespace: enterprise_docs_redis
type: Opaque
stringData:
  # Never commit real values - populate via \`kubectl create secret\` or a secrets manager.
  REDIS_PASSWORD: "REPLACE_ME"",
  },
  "rollback": [
    "Never run a destructive rollback step (dropping a table/collection, deleting a cluster) without explicit, out-of-band confirmation - the adapter layer refuses drop operations unless confirm=true is passed deliberately.",
    "Prefer disabling traffic to the new schema/collection (feature flag or app-config rollback) over deleting data, so the failed deployment can be inspected afterward.",
    "Roll back with \`helm rollback <release> <previous-revision>\` rather than deleting the namespace.",
    "If only the collection’s/index's configuration is at fault, drop and recreate just the index rather than the collection.",
  ],
  "terraform": "# STARTING POINT - provisions the Kubernetes cluster redis will run on.
# Fill in node sizing/count and networking for your cloud provider before applying.
resource "google_container_cluster" "golden_master_project" {
  name     = "golden_master_project-redis"
  location = var.gcp_region

  node_pool {
    name       = "redis-pool"
    node_count = var.node_count
    node_config {
      machine_type = var.machine_type
    }
  }
}

variable "gcp_region" {
  type = string
}
variable "node_count" {
  type    = number
  default = 3
}
variable "machine_type" {
  type    = string
  default = "e2-standard-8"
}

# Deploy redis itself onto this cluster with Helm/K8s YAML - see the generated Kubernetes artifacts.",
}
`;

exports[`Golden master - existing VectorDB workflow (must not change unintentionally) Phase 5 - deployment artefacts for every platform IaC and runbooks: weaviate 1`] = `
{
  "checklist": [
    "Provision the Kubernetes cluster via the generated Terraform (or an existing cluster).",
    "Create the namespace and secrets from the generated Kubernetes YAML.",
    "\`helm install\` (or apply the custom resource, for Elasticsearch/ECK) using the generated values file.",
    "Wait for all pods to reach Ready.",
    "Confirm TARGET_* connection environment variables are set via a secret manager, never committed to source control.",
    "Verify network connectivity (VPC peering / security group / firewall rule, or API reachability for a SaaS platform) from the application to the target database.",
    "Run the health check below and confirm it passes before creating any schema.",
    "Apply the generated schema/config (table + vector index, or collection/index config) exactly as reviewed - do not hand-edit generated identifiers.",
    "Re-run the health check after schema creation to confirm the database is still reachable and responsive.",
    "Record this deployment (version, rules version, timestamp) in the audit trail before marking Phase 4 complete.",
  ],
  "healthCheck": {
    "check": "GET /v1/.well-known/ready",
    "description": "Call Weaviate's readiness endpoint and confirm a 200 response.",
  },
  "kubernetes": {
    "helmValuesYaml": "# Values for the official \`weaviate/weaviate\` Helm chart (helm repo add weaviate https://weaviate.github.io/weaviate-helm).
# helm install enterprise_docs_weaviate weaviate/weaviate -n enterprise_docs_weaviate -f these-values.yaml
replicas: 3
storage:
  size: 50Gi
authentication:
  apikey:
    enabled: true
    existingSecret: weaviate-auth
modules:
  default_vectorizer_module: none # embeddings come from this platform's Phase 2 embedding model choice",
    "namespaceYaml": "apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: enterprise_docs_weaviate",
    "notes": [
      "replicas and storage size are starting points - size per the Phase 3 index choice and expected vector count/QPS.",
      "default_vectorizer_module is "none" because this platform supplies vectors at upsert time rather than having Weaviate compute them.",
    ],
    "secretYaml": "apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: weaviate-auth
  namespace: enterprise_docs_weaviate
type: Opaque
stringData:
  # Never commit real values - populate via \`kubectl create secret\` or a secrets manager.
  AUTHENTICATION_APIKEY_ALLOWED_KEYS: "REPLACE_ME"",
  },
  "rollback": [
    "Never run a destructive rollback step (dropping a table/collection, deleting a cluster) without explicit, out-of-band confirmation - the adapter layer refuses drop operations unless confirm=true is passed deliberately.",
    "Prefer disabling traffic to the new schema/collection (feature flag or app-config rollback) over deleting data, so the failed deployment can be inspected afterward.",
    "Roll back with \`helm rollback <release> <previous-revision>\` rather than deleting the namespace.",
    "If only the collection’s/index's configuration is at fault, drop and recreate just the index rather than the collection.",
  ],
  "terraform": "# STARTING POINT - provisions the Kubernetes cluster weaviate will run on.
# Fill in node sizing/count and networking for your cloud provider before applying.
resource "google_container_cluster" "golden_master_project" {
  name     = "golden_master_project-weaviate"
  location = var.gcp_region

  node_pool {
    name       = "weaviate-pool"
    node_count = var.node_count
    node_config {
      machine_type = var.machine_type
    }
  }
}

variable "gcp_region" {
  type = string
}
variable "node_count" {
  type    = number
  default = 3
}
variable "machine_type" {
  type    = string
  default = "e2-standard-8"
}

# Deploy weaviate itself onto this cluster with Helm/K8s YAML - see the generated Kubernetes artifacts.",
}
`;

